GPS character-device module for the native connectivity source build.

The MT6755 build uses stp_chrdev_gps.c. Module initialization returns the
character-device initialization error and releases resources acquired before
the failure. Its locks and wakeup source are ready before cdev_add() makes the
device reachable.

The host regression in ../common/test/test_chrdev_init.py exercises startup
failure and normal teardown without loading the module. See ../common/README
for the command and coverage. Firmware, calibration, and the GNSS HAL remain
separate runtime dependencies described in ../README.md.

If STP is not ready after WMT enables GPS, open unregisters its reset callback,
requests function-off, and restores the closed/reset state before returning
-ENODEV. A failed function-off request is logged; it does not turn the failed
open into success. The current callback registration implementations have no
failure path for the fixed GPS identifiers: WMT returns TRUE and STP returns 0.

From the kernel root, run the transport rollback/retry regression with:

  python3 drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/source/common/test/test_gps_open.py

It extracts GPS_open/GPS_close and checks readiness failure, reset arrival,
failed power rollback, successful retry, the function-on failure path, and
normal teardown. --revision REF runs those checks against committed source.
